class jadx.core.utils.EncodedValueUtils {
@Nullable
	public static Object convertToConstValue(EncodedValue encodedValue) {
		if (encodedValue == null) {
			return null;
		}
		Object value = encodedValue.getValue();
		switch (encodedValue.getType()) {
			case ENCODED_NULL:
				return InsnArg.lit(0, ArgType.OBJECT);
			case ENCODED_BOOLEAN:
				return Boolean.TRUE.equals(value) ? LiteralArg.litTrue() : LiteralArg.litFalse();
			case ENCODED_BYTE:
				return InsnArg.lit((Byte) value, ArgType.BYTE);
			case ENCODED_SHORT:
				return InsnArg.lit((Short) value, ArgType.SHORT);
			case ENCODED_CHAR:
				return InsnArg.lit((Character) value, ArgType.CHAR);
			case ENCODED_INT:
				return InsnArg.lit((Integer) value, ArgType.INT);
			case ENCODED_LONG:
				return InsnArg.lit((Long) value, ArgType.LONG);
			case ENCODED_FLOAT:
				return InsnArg.lit(Float.floatToIntBits((Float) value), ArgType.FLOAT);
			case ENCODED_DOUBLE:
				return InsnArg.lit(Double.doubleToLongBits((Double) value), ArgType.DOUBLE);
			case ENCODED_STRING:
				// noinspection RedundantCast
				return (String) value;

			case ENCODED_TYPE:
				return ArgType.parse((String) value);

			default:
				return null;
		}
}
}
```


### Response Format:

**If the method CANNOT return null at this specific call site:**
```xml
<response>
  <reason><![CDATA[EXPLAIN WHY THE INVOCATION ArgType arrType = ArgType.parse(insn.getIndexAsType()) RESULT CANNOT BE NULL.]]></reason>
  <value>NO</value>
</response>
```

**If the method CAN return null at this specific call site:**
```xml
<response>
  <reason><![CDATA[EXPLAIN WHY THE INVOCATION ArgType arrType = ArgType.parse(insn.getIndexAsType()) RESULT CAN BE NULL.]]></reason>
  <value>YES</value>
</response>
```

**If you need declarations of other methods to make a determination:**
```xml
<response>
  <reason><![CDATA[Explain why you need these method declarations to make a confident decision]]></reason>
  <success>false</success>
  <methods>
    <method>methodName</method>
  </methods>
</response>
```

### Important Notes:
- Be precise and specific in your reasoning
- If the method's return value depends on another method not provided, request its declaration
- If the method can return null in some cases but not this one, explain why this specific invocation is different

